  "content_en": "Chapter 1 First Marriage in the Prince's Mansion Ever since the last time he had a close encounter with an assassin, Prince Yu warned Luo Xue to be careful and told Xi Yi to guard Luo Xue. Therefore, every time Luo Xue leaves the small building in the center of the lake, there is always Xiao happy on the left and Xi Yi on the right. Wherever she went, there were surprised looks from the servants, which made Luo Xue very uncomfortable. She simply stayed in the small building and did not go out. She was really bored and panicked, so she went to Yanshu to chat and relieve her boredom. What's touching is that the gentle Yan Shu never minds these trivial things. The sharp spring breeze has become softer with the change of seasons, so soft that wherever it blows, it is full of life. But it was not something Luo Xue could enjoy. She sat in front of the mirror, brushed the red mark left by the burn on her forehead with her hand, and thought deeply: Luo Shang, aunt, where are you all? The past reappeared: young Luo Xue took her younger sister Luo Shang and ran all the way. I don’t know how long I ran, but I ran from dusk to dawn. It was a time of war, and no matter how long I ran, I was surrounded by a desolate scene. Panic, hunger, fatigue... the unfamiliar words appeared one by one and made Luo Xue understand it deeply, until she could no longer run. There were old, weak, sick and disabled people everywhere, gathering together, whining in pain and complaining. Luo Xue hugged Luo Shang tightly, but her body was shaking unconsciously. \"Sister, I'm hungry.\" Luo Shang whispered in Luo Xue's arms. I have been hungry for three days. My sister's physical condition is not good. How can she not eat? \"Luo Shang, be good, sister, go find something to eat.\" Luo Xue let go of Luo Shang and carefully stepped over the bodies of people sitting or lying on the ground. Where is there anything to eat? If so, will it be her turn? Thinking of this, Luo Xue shed tears. \"Sister, what's wrong with you? Luo Shang is scared and wants to go with you.\" The little Luo Shang pulled Luo Xue's sleeve and begged. Luo Xue wiped away her tears with her sleeves, forced a smile, and said, \"Okay, let's go together. Let's go to the mountain to find some fruits.\" Along the way, Luo Xue held Luo Shang's little hand and walked towards the mountain. She had already prepared for the worst when she gave the butterfly incense to Luo Shang. She told Luo Shang that when she really didn't want to live anymore, she would eat it. \"Sister, did you hear the sound?\" Luo Shang stopped and looked ahead. Luo Xue stopped and listened quietly. It was the first time she heard \"Butterfly Sorrow\". \"It's so sad.\" The tune of \"Butterfly Sorrow\" evoked Luo Chang's longing for her relatives. She said with tears in her eyes: \"Sister, I miss my father and mother.\" \"Shang'er, don't cry, my father and mother are looking at us.\" As she said this, she shed tears unsatisfactorily. \"Sister, let's not cry. Father and mother don't like us crying.\" Luo Shang wiped away Luo Xue's tears with her little hands. \"Sister, I'm hungry.\" \"Let's go find something to eat!\" She encouraged herself, took Luo Shang's hand, and continued walking forward. However, the sad music ahead was getting closer and closer, and the clearer sound made Luo Xue slow down. \"Who? Who is there!\" an alert male voice shouted angrily. The timid Luo Shang hurriedly got behind Luo Xue to protect her sister. Luo Xue told herself not to be afraid. She stood there without moving, and the unknown fear in front seemed to be close at hand. I saw a boy in ragged clothes walking from the front, with a very inappropriate flute tied to his side. \"What was I doing at that time? They turned out to be two children!\" \"Children? We are not!\" The boy in front of him was only a teenager, so he dared to act old in front of him? \"They look very similar to each other, just in time to cook me dinner!\" The boy laughed wildly. Luo Xue hurriedly protected Luo Shang, and bravely said loudly: \"It's not certain who will eat who!\" \"Then I'll eat you first.\" \"How dare you!\" \"You... behind...\" The boy pointed behind her. \"Stop bluffing me!\" \"Oh, I said the little girl behind you fainted!\" He immediately turned around and found that Luo Shang had fallen to the ground. \"Shang'er, what's wrong with you?\" He patted his sister's face with his hand, worried that something might happen to her, and tears of disappointment suddenly fell again. \"Let me see!\" The boy walked up to Luo Xue and wanted to pull her away. The stubborn Luo Xue was afraid that he would be harmful to Luo Shang, so she said fiercely: \"You don't have to worry about it!\" The boy scratched his messy hair, \"I was teasing you just now. Please tell me to see her!\" Then, he took Luo Shang from Luo Xue's arms and put his hand under Luo Shang's nose, \"You are still alive, maybe you are hungry!\" \"Hungry...\" Knowing that her sister had fainted from hunger, Luo Xue suddenly felt that sheVery useless, can't even take care of my sister well. \"Come, help me carry her to the river, and get her some water to drink first.\" The boy said, carrying Luo Shang on his back, and walked towards the river step by step. Luo Shang, who was semi-conscious, realized that she was being carried on someone's back. Although this person's back was not as wide or as strong as her father's, it made her feel warm and safe, safe enough to close her eyes and take a nap. The boy put Luo Shang under a big tree and asked her to lean against the trunk. \"Okay, let's ask her to sleep here for a while. Let's go catch fish and eat them when she wakes up, so that she can have strength.\" \"Catch fish? How to catch it?\" Luo Xue, who had never done menial work before, didn't know what to do. The boy was helpless, \"Of course I'll catch it with my hands. Do you want her to starve to death?\" After hearing that her sister would starve to death, Luo Xue bit her lip, took off her shoes, rolled up her trouser legs, walked to the river, rolled up her sleeves, bent down and grabbed with her hands, but she caught nothing for a long time. She looked up at the boy on the shore asking her to catch fish, only to find that he was cutting the head off a branch with a knife. \"Hey, aren't you catching fish? What are you doing?\" The boy put down what he was doing and asked curiously: \"What are you doing in the river?\" \"Catch fish!\" \"Catch fish? Haha\" the boy laughed, and after a while he covered his stomach and laughed even more wildly. \"Catch fish! Haha\" \"What's wrong? Didn't you tell me to catch fish? Didn't you say to use your hands?\" Luo Xue stood in the river, wondering why he smiled so brightly. The boy stopped laughing. He picked up the two branches he had just cut, walked to Luo Xue, and handed one to Luo Xue, \"Look, you can catch it with your hands like this!\" As he said, he put up the branch. When he saw the fish swimming towards him, he thrust hard and lifted it up. A crucian carp that was shaking its head and tail and struggling for death was nailed to the branch. \"How's it going? You're awesome! Let's learn from it!\" Luo Xue, who was not willing to give in easily, followed his example and fucked her. But being a skilled fisherman after all, it took him the third time to insert the fish. Luo Xue, who had tasted success for the first time, got interested and inserted six more fish in a row. \"Don't stick it in, you won't be able to eat it. Buddha said that saving a life is better than building a seven-level pagoda.\" The boy, who was already squatting on the shore, picked up some small branches and piled them into a small pile. \"What are you doing?\" Luo Xue walked to the shore, wiped her feet with her sleeves, and put on her shoes. \"Let's light a fire. How about grilling the fish? Did you see the sharpened branches on the ground? Put the harpoon on and let's grill the fish.\" Luo Xue leaned over, picked up the small branches, walked to the dead fish, sat down, and began to thread the fish. The bonfire was lit and the rack for grilling fish was set up. Luo Xue took the dressed fish and prepared to put it on the fire. \"Wait a minute!\" the boy stopped. \"What's wrong?\" \"The gall is not taken care of, I'll be careful to kill you.\" The boy took out his knife and carefully removed the gall from each fish, then put it on the fire with confidence and started roasting it with concentration, without anyone saying anything else. Luo Xue picked a larger leaf, filled it with some water, and carefully dripped it on Luo Shang's dry mouth. I don’t know how long it took, but the aroma of the fish gradually dissipated. \"Okay, let's wake her up.\" The boy walked to Luo Xue and handed Luo Xue two branches with cooked fish on them. She took it and gently shook Luo Shang awake, \"Sister, get up and eat.\" \"Eat?\" Luo Shang rubbed her sleepy eyes, took the fish, and asked, \"Where did it come from?\" Luo Xue pointed to the boy who was already sitting in front of the fire, \"It's him.\" \"Oh.\" What appeared in front of Luo Shang was a thin back figure. Although thin and unable to see his face, she was sure that the person carrying her just now was him. After eating the fish, Luo Shang went to sleep. Her body was too weak, maybe she could make up for it by sleeping. Luo Xue took off her coat and put it on Luo Shang, then walked to the fire and asked, \"Is that the tune you played just now?\" \"Well, this is the only tune I know. My name is A Ran, what is your name?\" Luo Xue paused, \"My name is A Xue, and that is my sister, A Shang.\" Although the boy in front of her helped her, she still had to be defensive, so Luo Xue did not tell her and her sister's real names. \"Where are you going?\" \"I don't know.\" Looking at the dark night sky in the distance, Aran smiled, \"With the chaos of war, who knows where you are going?\" \"What is the name of the song you are playing?\" \"\"Butterfly Sorrow\"\" After saying that, he took out his flute and started playing. Luo Xue stood by quietly, not knowing when she fell asleep. When she woke up, it was already dawn. Next to her was Luo Shang, who was sleeping soundly. Not far away were the remains of the extinguished fire, but there was no trace of A Ran.I felt secretly disappointed in my heart. \"Are you awake?\" A Ran came over holding a few green fruits in his hands. The joy from an unknown place drove away the gloom in Luo Xue's heart, \"I'm going to wash my face.\" \"I'm going to wash these fruits with you.\" When she came to the river, Luo Xue held water in her hands and patted her face repeatedly. When she thought it was clean, she wiped it dry with her sleeves. She turned her head to look at A Ran, but saw A Ran looking at her, \"What are you looking at?\" \"You are so beautiful!\" A Ran said truthfully. Luo Xue smiled. If it were anyone else, she would probably be fierce with him, but towards A Ran, Luo Xue couldn't be fierce, probably because he had saved Luo Shang. \"Sister, where are you?\" Luo Shang's anxious voice came from the distance. \"Here, coming.\" He quickly ran to Luo Shang. \"Where are we going soon?\" Luo Shang stood up. \"I don't know,\" Luo Xue said, looking at A Ran who was still by the river, \"Follow him.\" \"Who is he?\" \"His name is A Ran!\" \"Will he agree?\" Luo Xue shouted hard to A Ran: \"A Ran, do you agree that we go together?\" A Ran stretched his body and said, \"I have no objection!\" So the three of them began their journey together. They were walking on a mountain road. The mountains in Yunnan are rich. No matter how long they walked, they would not go hungry. Aran told them that if they walked further, they would reach Dali, which should not have been captured by the barbarians. Three hearts that had also suffered, supported each other and moved forward together. It was quite lively along the way. They were talking and laughing, which made them all forget the unpleasantness caused by the war. Of course, it was just Luo Xue and A Ran who were talking, while Luo Shang was listening quietly.",
